# The Pixel 9a's declaration that suspend with the modem up works, as
# device-cheetah's is for the Pixel 7 Pro. On W4HO-ham's 9a, under #809's
# terms: the modem-up series of #837 (20 of 20 sleeps entered and woke, mobile
# data back after each) and a night on the shell's own path on 2026-11-20 (32
# sleeps through omamobile-sleepd and logind, the longest 50 minutes, no
# service watchdog line, no UFS error line), both with the modem's sleep
# inhibitor lifted by hand. With this file omamobile-modem's sleep policy
# says yes, and omamobile-tegu-modem-up then takes no sleep inhibitor, but
# only on a kernel whose modem link refuses a sleep early while the link is up
# (linux-omamobile#232, kernel-2026.11.15 and later), and not where the owner
# has opted out (/etc/omamobile/modem-suspend-disable, from the next boot).
